# Personal Website Project Rules

## Project Purpose

This repository contains my personal portfolio website hosted on GitHub Pages.

The purpose of this site is:

* showcase projects
* host a personal blog
* centralize social/media links
* document learning and experiments
* act as a public technical portfolio

The site should remain lightweight, fast, maintainable, and easy to understand.

---

# Core Philosophy

Prefer:

* simplicity
* readability
* maintainability
* clean architecture
* low dependency count
* static hosting compatibility

Avoid:

* unnecessary abstraction
* overengineering
* excessive dependencies
* backend services
* unnecessary frameworks
* premature optimization

---

# Technical Constraints

Use:

* HTML
* CSS
* minimal vanilla JavaScript

Avoid unless explicitly requested:

* React
* Next.js
* Node backends
* databases
* authentication systems
* APIs
* large UI frameworks

The site should work by simply opening index.html locally.

---

# Design Direction

The design should feel:

* modern
* minimal
* technical
* professional
* personal
* clean

Preferred:

* dark theme
* responsive layouts
* subtle styling
* semantic HTML
* accessible structure

Avoid:

* flashy animations
* clutter
* excessive gradients
* overly corporate styling

---

# Site Structure

Core pages:

* Home
* About
* Projects
* Blog
* Contact

Blog implementation:

* static HTML posts
* no CMS
* no backend

Projects page:

* simple project cards
* GitHub links
* concise descriptions

---

# Coding Style

Code should be:

* beginner-readable
* well commented where necessary
* modular but simple
* easy to extend later

CSS should:

* use reusable classes
* avoid unnecessary nesting
* stay organized and readable

JavaScript should:

* remain minimal
* avoid unnecessary libraries
* prioritize clarity

---

# Deployment

The site is intended for:

* GitHub Pages hosting

Ensure:

* relative paths work correctly
* pages are static-host compatible
* deployment remains simple

---

# AI Assistant Instructions

When making suggestions:

* prefer the simplest viable solution
* explain major decisions briefly
* do not introduce complexity without justification
* optimize for long-term maintainability

Do not transform this project into a large web application unless explicitly instructed.
